police in Bermuda are not ruling out  foul play in the mysterious death of an  American college student the body of 19  year old Mark Dombrowski was found on  the island yesterday  the freshman rugby player was last seen  early Sunday after his team competed in  a tournament teammates at st. Joseph's  University in Philadelphia gathered  yesterday to grieve and a Warner is at  the college campus in Philadelphia where  people are said to be shaken by their  loss and a good morning good morning  well mark Dombrowski left this campus  last week bound for Bermuda the plan was  for him to play for the first time ever  on the school's rugby sevens team there  but Sunday morning his family reported  him missing it was the day of his return  flight that set off a frantic search  that ended in tragedy we loved him  dearly we want him back Linda Dombrowski  had pleaded for her son's safe return  but Monday it became clear mark  Dombrowski would not be coming back  police found his body in a wooded area  near Fort Prospect a colonial-era  military garrison outside bermudez  capital Hamilton police have not yet  released any details about how the 19  year old died foul play is not ruled out  right now the forensic officers are  there they're assessing the scene  assessing the body Dombrowski played on  the st. Joseph's varsity rugby team and  was in Bermuda for a tournament  investigators say Saturday night after  their final game he and his teammates  went to a bar in Hamilton called the dog  house there's no information to suggest  at the moment that he himself was  intoxicated or that alcohol is a part  police say Dombrowski left the bar  shortly after midnight Sunday at 1:09  a.m. a security camera spotted him about  four blocks away alone and using his  cell phone he showed up in another  surveillance video about six minutes  later the site where his body was found  is near Bermudas police headquarters as  well as the Sports Center where the  rugby tournament was held we expect an  autopsy to be carried out in due course  we spoke with some of his friends last  night at the memorial service at a  church near here and they remembered a  young man John full of energy and  promise and one who will be sorely  missed you know thanks
 

